# EPDS — Component Conventions

## File layout
Every component lives in its own folder under `src/components/ComponentName/`:

```
src/components/ComponentName/
  ComponentName.vue
  ComponentName.stories.ts
  index.ts
```

The component's `index.ts` re-exports the SFC default and any public types.

## Library export
After adding a component, **register it in `src/index.ts`** so it ships in `dist/epds.js`. Also re-export shared types the same way as existing entries.

## SFC rules
- Use `<script setup lang="ts">`, `defineProps<{}>()`, `defineEmits<{}>()` — **no Options API**
- `<style scoped>` only — no global selectors in component files
- No inline styles unless dynamically computed
- BEM-style class names rooted on the component (e.g. `accordion`, `accordion__header`, `accordion__header--open`)

## Reuse first
Before writing new markup, check whether an existing component (`BaseButton`, `LinkCta`, `Alert`, `Accordion`, etc.) already fits. **Do not** add hidden one-off primitives inside larger components without explicit sign-off.

## No new sub-components without checking the user
If a composite needs a new primitive, propose it first. The catalog rules (atoms/molecules/organisms) are the source of truth for what's already built — fetch them when unsure.

## Vue + TypeScript template gotcha
On child SFCs, bind props using the **camelCase name from `defineProps`** — `vue-tsc` treats DOM-style `aria-label` as a separate attribute and will report required props missing.

```vue
<!-- BAD: vue-tsc will complain ariaLabel is missing -->
<MediumIconButton aria-label="Open menu" />

<!-- GOOD -->
<MediumIconButton :aria-label="'Open menu'" />
<!-- or just -->
<MediumIconButton ariaLabel="Open menu" />
```

## Vue + TypeScript: typed union for input modes
On `TextField` and similar inputs, `inputmode` is a **typed union**, not a plain `string`. Use the typed prop value — `vue-tsc` flags `string` as too wide.

## Brand awareness
Components themselves are usually brand-agnostic. Brand-specific values come through CSS custom properties — see the `tokens.mdc` rule for the three-layer architecture and white-label pattern. When a component needs brand-specific structural overrides (e.g. Sonic-only hover underline on `BaseButton` secondary), scope them with `[data-brand="sonic"]`.

## When to update the catalog
When you add a new component, update the matching catalog rule (`atoms-catalog.mdc` / `molecules-catalog.mdc` / `organisms-catalog.mdc`) in the same change. The catalogs are the project's component memory — they stay current only if updates are paired with code.
